# Build inputs the image does not need, and secrets it must never contain.

# Secrets. The keys live in `fly secrets`, never in a layer — an image is not private,
# and a leaked layer cannot be un-leaked by rotating the file.
.env
.env.*
.certs

# Rebuilt inside the container.
node_modules
build
out

# Not needed to build the wizard, the server, or the render bundle.
skills
docs
test_792.png
test_1420_new.png
video-customizer-reveal-dark.html

# A finished render left in the repo root — 102 MB, and over half of what every deploy
# uploaded to the builder. Nothing serves it: the server mounts build/ and public/, and
# this is in neither. It was the largest single item in a 181 MB build context.
workvivo-dewalt.mp4

# The original L2 edit, in both its encodes: 310 MB of master and 45 MB of CRF 24
# re-encode. NEITHER is loaded at render time any more. Every one of the film's 5300
# frames is drawn by a scene now — verified by rendering the whole thing with the
# reference replaced by a marker colour and finding none of it left — and the only thing
# the video was still carrying, its audio track, is extracted to
# public/audio/l2-soundtrack.m4a and played from there. See the note on SOUNDTRACK in
# src/WorkvivoCut.tsx.
#
# They stay in the REPO because every scene's numbers were measured off them and the prep
# scripts still read them; they are simply not build inputs.
public/img/L2 Video(Virgin Airline).mp4
public/img/l2-reference-212s.mp4

# The old 54-second trim, from when the customised cut stopped at frame 1350. Nothing
# references it now that the wizard runs the whole film.
public/img/l2-reference-54s.mp4

# Design references: the HTML captures the Workvivo screens were ported FROM, plus a
# 15 MB library zip. Useful in the repo, dead weight in the image.
public/refs

# Duplicate of webinar.mp4 with a typo'd name, referenced by nothing.
public/img/webianr.mp4

.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.claude
web/**/*.test.*

# Audio build inputs for the Japanese cut. The image needs the finished mix
# (public/audio/japanese-soundtrack.mp3, 5 MB) and none of what it was made from: the music
# stem alone is 42 MB. Rebuild them with scripts/build-japanese-vo.mjs, which is a
# development step, not a deploy one.
public/audio/Quantum_Flow.wav
public/audio/VO.mp3
public/audio/japanese-voiceover.mp3
public/audio/japanese-voiceover-paced.mp3
public/audio/japanese-voiceover-v1.mp3
public/audio/japanes-voiceover-2.mp3
